From: mjbommar <michael.bommarito@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 22:06:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH bpf-next 0/2] bpf, x86: two hygiene fixes in bpf_jit_comp.c
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two small hygiene cleanups in arch/x86/net/bpf_jit_comp.c. Both
are zero-functional-change on x86 defconfig (bpf_jit_comp.o byte-
for-byte size unchanged in my testing); they make the TU's
dependencies more explicit and migrate two direct pt_regs field
accesses to the generic helpers that kprobes, uprobes, and ftrace
already use.

Patch 1 — "bpf, x86: explicitly include <asm/cpufeature.h>"

  bpf_jit_comp.c calls boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_BMI2) and
  cpu_feature_enabled(X86_FEATURE_INDIRECT_THUNK_ITS) without an
  explicit include of <asm/cpufeature.h>. On x86 defconfig the
  declarations are available transitively through
  <asm/nospec-branch.h>; under thinner include-path arrangements
  the chain can drop them and the build fails at
  bpf_jit_comp.c:1997 ("implicit declaration of function
  'boot_cpu_has'") and at :676 (DISABLED_MASK_BIT_SET implicit
  declaration via the cpu_feature_enabled expansion).

  Making the dependency explicit is a pure-hygiene fix.

Patch 2 — "bpf, x86: use instruction_pointer helpers in
          ex_handler_bpf"

  The arena-access exception handler accesses the trapped PC via
  regs->ip directly (once to report, once to skip the faulting
  instruction). Convert both sites to instruction_pointer() and
  instruction_pointer_set(); these are static-always-inline
  wrappers in arch/x86/include/asm/ptrace.h that compile to the
  same field access on x86. Matches the pattern used across the
  tree (kprobes, uprobes, ftrace) for pt_regs PC access.

Both patches compile clean on x86_64 defconfig + BPF_JIT=y; they
do not change emitted JIT code or the kernel ABI.

No Fixes: tag — these predate any recent regression and both
files have been stable for many cycles. Please consider for
bpf-next.

mjbommar (2):
  bpf, x86: explicitly include <asm/cpufeature.h>
  bpf, x86: use instruction_pointer helpers in ex_handler_bpf

 arch/x86/net/bpf_jit_comp.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

